  "metadata": {
    "title": "RuralDrone5G_RadioLatencyDataset",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.16673883",
    "publication_date": "2025-08-01",
    "description": "<p>The dataset comprises&nbsp; CSV files, each representing a different measurement iteration labeled from <code>fligth1</code> to <code>fligth5</code>. These files collectively form a comprehensive dataset of radio network parameters, likely derived from performance monitoring in the 5G SA private network deployed in the experimental farm La Mayora, M&aacute;laga, Spain. This 5G private network is part of the Victoria Network experimentation platform. The measurements have been collected using a Nemo Handy onboarded in a drone.</p>\n<p>The NR band used is \"NR n40 TDD\".</p>\n<p>The files include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Physical layer parameters</strong> such as BWP ID, BWP type, bandwidth, numerology, subcarrier spacing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Radio quality indicators</strong> including RSRP, RSRQ, SINR.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>HARQ and MIMO configurations</strong>, scheduling information, and potentially signaling or decoding parameters.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Timestamps (<code>Time</code>)</strong> that allow tracking the temporal progression of each measurement session.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Dronetelemetry</strong></li>\n</ul>",
